{%- comment -%}
  Google Search Console ownership verification.

  Search Console asks the site to prove ownership by serving a meta tag in
  the <head> of the home page. The merchant pastes the token under
  Theme settings → Google Search Console and it is rendered here on every
  page, in both layouts, so it is also found while the store is password
  protected.

  Google hands out the whole <meta name="google-site-verification" ...> tag,
  and pasting that is the natural thing to do, so a pasted tag is reduced to
  its content value rather than rendered as a tag inside a tag.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign gsc_token = settings.google_site_verification | strip

  if gsc_token contains 'content='
    assign gsc_token = gsc_token | split: 'content="' | last | split: '"' | first
  endif
-%}

{%- if gsc_token != blank -%}
  <meta name="google-site-verification" content="{{ gsc_token | strip | escape }}">
{%- endif -%}
